## Allow graph refreshes on published domain versions

Context: Issue #78 remained reproducible in the UI after a later view-mode
permission change reconnected Build and reasoning materialisation to ontology
editability. The backend already treats these operations as data refreshes.
Builders can now refresh graph data from a frozen IN-REVIEW or PUBLISHED design
without reopening that version for editing.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/global/js/permissions.js`
   Added a builder-level graph-refresh permission independent of lifecycle status while preserving edit-lock enforcement.
2. `src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css`
   Removed lifecycle read-only gating from Build and reasoning materialisation while retaining viewer and edit-lock gates.
3. `src/front/static/query/js/query-sync.js`
   Applied the graph-refresh permission consistently and skipped the domain save step when building a frozen version.
4. `src/front/static/query/js/query-reasoning.js`
   Allowed builders to materialise reasoning results on frozen versions.
5. `tests/units/front/test_view_mode_write_gates.py`
   Added regression coverage for lifecycle-independent refresh permissions, view-mode gates, and the frozen-version save bypass.
6. `documentation/user-guide.md`
   Documented that builders and admins can refresh graph data on IN-REVIEW and PUBLISHED versions.
7. `README.md`
   Clarified the lifecycle behavior of the Build workflow.

