## Name the storage kind on Knowledge Graph → Build, and harden the feature's tests

Context: with Lakehouse view-only materialization shipped, the Build page still
described its target as a "Delta table" in the places it had not been made
mode-aware — the page subtitle and the target FQN block. Same FQN, very
different behaviour: a materialized copy is a point-in-time snapshot refreshed
only by a build, a view is always live and its triple count is a live query.
Someone landing on the page could not tell which one they had without opening
Domain → Information.

The feature's test coverage also had gaps at the edges: the two payloads that
report the mode (task result, audited build run), the two read APIs that expose
it (`settings_health_summary`, `/dtwin/databricks-build/info`), and the whole
UI wiring were untested.

Changes:

1. `src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_databricks_build.html`
   Added `#dbxBuildStorageBadge` next to the target label, `#dbxBuildStorageNote`
   under the FQN, and an id on the page subtitle so JS can rewrite it. Replaced
   the stale "Delta TABLE only" file comment.
2. `src/front/static/query/js/query-databricks-build.js`
   New `_applyDbxStorageKind(isViewMode)` centralises every mode-dependent
   string: label, badge (`TABLE · materialized copy` / `VIEW · no data copy`
   with tooltip), explanatory note, and subtitle. Status card title shortened to
   `View status`. Info tint for the view (the deliberate, non-default choice),
   neutral for the table — primary red stays reserved per `.cursor/11`.
3. `src/front/static/query/js/query-databricks-build.js` (bug fix)
   `count` was declared with `const` inside `if (statusCard)` but read in the
   `statusText` block below it — a `ReferenceError` whenever `has_data` was
   truthy, i.e. on every domain with triples. Hoisted alongside `isViewMode`.
4. `src/front/static/query/css/query-sync.css`
   Added `.dbx-storage-badge` so the badge sizing is not an inline `style`.
5. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaTripleStoreBuildPipeline.py`
   Module docstring said "R2RML VIEW → materialized Delta TABLE"; it now builds
   either relation.
6. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   `databricks_build_info` docstring said "Delta table status" and did not
   mention the `materialization` field it returns.
7. `tests/units/front/test_lakehouse_materialization_ui.py` (new, 26 tests)
   UI contracts: the picker (rendered through Jinja, so the backend gating and
   the default selection are asserted as behaviour rather than as source text),
   the toggle wiring, both save paths including the off-Lakehouse reset, and the
   mode-aware labels on the health card and the Build page.
8. `tests/units/dtwin/test_databricks_build_info_materialization.py` (new, 4 tests)
   `/dtwin/databricks-build/info` through a real `TestClient` and a real
   `DomainSession`: both modes, the legacy default, and the non-Lakehouse guard.
9. `tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_materialize.py`
   Added `TestWhatABuildReports` — `build_mode`/`materialization` in the task
   result and in the registry build-run entry, including the zero-triple early
   exit, which has its own payload. Added a test that the progress step names the
   object it creates. `_StubTM` now records steps and results.
10. `tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_package.py`
    `settings_health_summary` reports the mode (both modes); analytics-snapshot
    naming rejects an unqualified view and is not derived from `…_data`. Stubbed
    `create_databricks_client` in the health tests, removing a
    `PytestUnraisableExceptionWarning` from the SQL connector dialing out with
    mock credentials.
11. `documentation/user-guide.md`
    Documented the storage-kind indicator under **Build (Sidebar)** with a
    per-mode comparison table.

